a safari in the pantanal the Earth's  largest tropical Wetlands tourists from  all over the world come to watch rare  birds and wildlife in the Brazilian  state of matogrosudu  two years ago a catastrophic fire  destroyed much of this green Paradise  leaving a trail of Destruction and  killing millions of native species  Farmers have always cleared their lands  with fire but the intensity of the fires  we've seen in the last year is not  common it's a consequence of the worst  drought in a century caused by  deforestation in the Amazon and  extensive farming  Brazil witnessed a peak of deforestation  in the Amazon in 2021 13 000 square  kilometers were destroyed reaching a  14-year High  environmentalists fear that if  bothordaro wins the October 30th runoff  he'll continue pushing for legislation  to open up protected areas for Mining  and farming as he said he would  president bolsonaro's government has  already dismantled and defunded public  organizations in charge of controlling  the preservation of the environment the  pantanal is the size of many European  countries if there's no protection it  will eventually dry out bolsonando's  left-wing rival Forum president luisi  nasululla Da Silva has been criticized  in the past for the construction of the  controversial Balo monche hydropower dam  in the Amazon it displaced some forty  thousand people  but Lola did Implement environmental  policies dramatically reducing  deforestation and is promising to  rebuild government institutions that  control illegal activities in the Amazon  judging how Brazilians voted in the  first round the environment is far from  being a priority  four out of every 10 congressmen elected  are against strict laws limiting  economic activity in protected areas  these charcoal colored tree trunks are  the scars of an intense fire that passed  through this Forest three years ago it  took firefighters 40 days to control the  flames and even though scarce rain  helped the pantanal flourish this may  well be a temporary respite the future  of the pantanal and the Amazon May well  depend on the outcome of Sunday's  election and on the capability of the  next president to find a balance between  defending nature while promoting much  needed economic growth Monica yanakev Al  Jazeera pantanau Brazil
 

